{"title":"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/8/ee87a6df3c99344984d21f25720b6c332f19dd59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1, b_1, a_2, b_2, \\dots , a_n, b_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"172\" height=\"16\" /> be nonnegative real numbers. Prove that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/9/f59aeb8ab929d8b6b14c2e3a997a43541a18c2c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i, j = 1}^{n} \\min\\{a_ia_j, b_ib_j\\} \\le \\sum_{i, j = 1}^{n} \\min\\{a_ib_j, a_jb_i\\}.\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>Credit for this solution goes to Ravi Boppana.</i>\n</p><p><b>Lemma 1:</b> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/d/8fd5a73488a86e9e6b012698b09b264491f896f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1, r_2, \\ldots , r_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"11\" /> are non-negative reals and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/d/aad197e79abc812b51e774fd24bd11f11681cd31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2, \\ldots x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"13\" /> are reals, then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47b088ac1888cca9bf515ed4260ebb3cced4d18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i, j}\\min(r_{i}, r_{j}) x_{i}x_{j}\\ge 0.\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><b>Proof:</b> Without loss of generality assume that the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/6/fa69872b32dc274f62a32e547822aaa7d04da244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{r_i\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is increasing. For convenience, define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0fa3426194a0dc57037b471c556d6d762d4b68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_0=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />. The LHS of our inequality becomes\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/e/23e1c5806c124fea0a85050c20bd7f61a222649e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i}r_{i}x_{i}^{2}+2\\sum_{i &lt; j}r_{i}x_{i}x_{j}\\, .\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>This expression is equivalent to the sum\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/5/b157a5bb705586c761c82b2ceab78c42a8915028.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i}(r_{i}-r_{i-1})\\biggl(\\sum_{j=i}^{n}x_{j}\\biggr)^{2}\\, .\\]\" width=\"192\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p>Each term in the summation is non-negative, so the sum itself is non-negative. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>We now define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec658d5f8b6af47d05d732f3244381ac726df06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_i=\\frac{\\max(a_i,b_i)}{\\min(a_i,b_i)}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"156\" height=\"43\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/8515d048be23979de833918d842aadf557d7a60d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min(a_i,b_i)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />, then let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c42077f2a447ca548cdbfe63f1932e9866df3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be any non-negative number. Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/9/b3980c640bd5c3c3548296830019db4c8b81041d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i=\\text{sgn}(a_i-b_i)\\min(a_i,b_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 2:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67aa681bbeba193d788af4fff164fac5bfbd9316.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min(a_{i}b_{j}, a_{j}b_{i})-\\min(a_{i}a_{j}, b_{i}b_{j}) =\\min(r_{i}, r_{j}) x_{i}x_{j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"384\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><b>Proof:</b> Switching the signs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" /> preserves inequality, so we may assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bf0b5901cb298528306d26c2c7f68ba806a2143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i&gt;b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />. Similarly, we can assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/03250a4ee70fb68f47f94b1e0ebea555c77af99b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_j&gt;b_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b7956f4c1358e149dee9110056aacf3b60300983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_ib_j=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, then both sides are zero, so we may assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/d/94d9565abaadf04609a2e9941aa2d20b0a299b8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfbbf3e10280b5771976f3342b10181e4b31d4fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"17\" /> are positive. We then have from the definitions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c42077f2a447ca548cdbfe63f1932e9866df3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b586187f7745f7e0573851b1b35a9b8f0f2f771.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}r_{i}&amp; = &amp;\\frac{a_{i}}{b_{i}}-1\\\\ r_{j}&amp; = &amp;\\frac{a_{j}}{b_{j}}-1\\\\ x_{i}&amp; = &amp; b_{i}\\\\ x_{j}&amp; = &amp; b_{j}\\, .\\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"115\" height=\"128\" />\n</p><p>This means that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/a/4ca661ebe830c3d7f6ff9c0bdbe5c012feb99127.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}\\min(r_{i}, r_{j}) x_{i}x_{j}&amp; = &amp;\\min\\bigl(\\frac{a_{i}}{b_{i}}-1,\\frac{a_{j}}{b_{j}}-1\\bigr) b_{i}b_{j}\\\\ &amp; = &amp;\\min(a_{i}b_{j}, a_{j}b_{i})-b_{i}b_{j}\\\\ &amp; = &amp;\\min(a_{i}b_{j}, a_{j}b_{i})-\\min(a_{i}a_{j}, b_{i}b_{j})\\, .\\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"415\" height=\"87\" />\n</p><p>This concludes the proof of Lemma 2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>We can then apply Lemma 2 and Lemma 1 in order to get that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/0/ac0d42b46e3418f4539d0ac6db051875d554f2fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{eqnarray*}\\sum_{i,j}\\min(a_{i}b_{j}, a_{j}b_{i})-\\sum_{i, j}\\min(a_{i}a_{j}, b_{i}b_{j}) &amp; = &amp;\\sum_{i, j}\\left[\\min(a_{i}b_{j}, a_{j}b_{i})-\\min(a_{i}a_{j}, b_{i}b_{j})\\right]\\\\ &amp; = &amp;\\sum_{i, j}\\min(r_{i}, r_{j}) x_{i}x_{j}\\\\ &amp;\\ge &amp; 0\\, .\\end{eqnarray*}\" width=\"635\" height=\"111\" />\n</p><p>This implies the desired inequality.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>WLOG let both sequences be increasing. Furthermore allow the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a0dd857eb1670b6e8dd4d9ecf3f6c6dcf79beb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i \\leq b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />. Hence, it is sufficient to show that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b3410ef1a2e2223b8bd552b20933df3f2fd14e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i,j = 1}^n a_ia_j \\leq \\sum_{i,j = 1}^n \\min(a_ib_j, a_jb_i)\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"50\" />. \n</p><p><b>Lemma 1:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/3226fdb426a5447aaf960ce433d6150b37bb2d47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min(a_ib_j, a_jb_i) =  a_ib_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"168\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc672a6e0a91e3e07a8a061ec6abedc9687964b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\leq j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><b>Proof of Lemma 1:</b>\n</p><p>Through the Rearrangement Inequality,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/757a568941cb0dba0521f186e394c4322462e447.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_i b_i+a_j b_j\\ge a_i b_j+a_j b_i\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/b/4eb7d3bc7d38466f23bfa0e582c108bfe7c42413.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_i b_i+a_j b_j-a_i b_j-a_j b_i\\ge0\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/554b23d806a8ffa45571e2880d714d24359e7249.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a_j-a_i)(b_j-b_i)\\ge0\\]\" width=\"164\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>As both sequences are increasing, the property holds.\n</p><p>(Note: A proof by contradiction of assuming that the other inequality is true derives the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba88da26dd41c984d3645a009027b5bdda55f3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i, b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is decreasing which goes against our WLOG).\n</p><p><b>Lemma 2:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/a/56a9de708681386032394068846c7d3f7c9a3fa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\min(a_ib_j, a_jb_i) =  a_jb_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"168\" height=\"20\" />  for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/1/23166a59a6df7d262929f4e7e4803c9da65e6504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i &gt; j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>For space reasons, the proof is similar to that of Lemma 1. \n</p><p><b>2000 USAMO Q6:</b>\n</p><p>Rewrite the sum as \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70da9b5550701c99ca27fcf6987e40eccf6b11ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i,j=1}^{n}\\min(a_i b_j,a_jb_i)=\\sum_{i=j}\\min(a_i b_i,a_i b_i)+\\sum_{i&lt;j}\\min(a_i b_j,a_jb_i)+\\sum_{i&gt;j}\\min(a_i b_j,a_jb_i)\\]\" width=\"618\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>Obviously, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> is even hence form the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> matrix. The RHS sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f250ad5597af423f5d8e0489735d28080f2195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i\\le j}a_i b_j+\\sum_{i&gt;j}a_jb_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"141\" height=\"45\" /> then satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/3/463d37617c74b52a8b551175bed028779cf6dd94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i&gt;j}a_jb_i=\\sum_{i&lt;j}a_i b_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"143\" height=\"45\" />. This is trivial by considering all values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/1348d0537427959d5c62bf272213904f848e5b31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_jb_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" /> below the diagonal of the matrix, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/d/f6d60ec0728566087c7dd05fca60f8420f299115.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_ib_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"32\" height=\"19\" /> above the diagonal, and all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dec6fefeed01bda2ebb538e01fae1eb53458cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_ib_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"17\" /> in the diagonal itself. It is then clear that the RHS simplifies to \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd845de3b202ce57f2c470ac29991b86f86f57de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_i a_i b_i+2\\sum_{i&lt;j}a_i b_j\\]\" width=\"148\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>Note that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/5/435e829fae2973f7b968eb15f218e598c3868d5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i,j=1}^n a_i a_j=\\sum_i a_i^2+2\\sum_{i&lt;j}a_i a_j\\]\" width=\"229\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a0dd857eb1670b6e8dd4d9ecf3f6c6dcf79beb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i \\leq b_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/6522876dbd067d61a4fd1fc4107f56ee587c3ce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i^2 \\leq a_ib_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"21\" /> via Rearrangement Inequality. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/478f5d7d31a103e7a383486cdf317eb599ac9ebf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i &lt; j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/9/2d91c390cc052dbae15ab37da254cb6bd48037dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_ia_j \\leq a_ib_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"88\" height=\"19\" /> by the Lemma's. Hence, through inequality equivalencies,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/d/52dd91c51d59d6d10010faef3089e8f06496e0b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_i a_i^2+2\\sum_{i&lt;j}a_i a_j\\le \\sum_i a_i b_i+2\\sum_{i&lt;j}a_i b_j\\]\" width=\"313\" height=\"39\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/1/c21de697765ad6745a5698166ba3b90927a4ae03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\iff  \\sum_{i,j=1}^n a_i a_j \\le \\sum_{i,j=1}^n\\min(a_i b_j,a_jb_i)\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>as desired. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO\" title=\"2000 USAMO\">2000 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2000\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2000 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017194400\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.067 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 318/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 55/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11118/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   18.401      1 -total\n 66.28%   12.197      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 32.02%    5.892      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11009:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017194400 and revision id 287608. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}